\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{3}{ The dual-stage knowledge distillation strategy for few-shot knowledge distillation. Firstly, student network $\mathcal  {S}$ is decomposed into several blocks: $\{h_l\}_{l=1}^L$, each of which is grafted onto teacher and then optimized by few-shot distillation between $\mathcal  {T}_l^{B}$ and $\mathcal  {T}$. Secondly, trained blocks in the first stage: $\{\mathcal  {H}_l\}_{l=1}^L$ are sequentially composed into the trained student network: $\mathcal  {S}$ using few-shot distillation between $\mathcal  {T}_l^{N}$ and $\mathcal  {T}$. }{}{}}
